berry for Debian
----------------

This package ships no configuration. berry is configured by an executable
autostart script, which it looks for at berry/autostart inside the XDG config
directory (usually ~/.config/berry/autostart), and it runs with compiled-in
defaults when that is absent.

Upstream's examples are installed at

  /usr/share/doc/berry/examples/autostart
  /usr/share/doc/berry/examples/sxhkdrc

Copy autostart to ~/.config/berry/autostart and make it executable. sxhkdrc is
for sxhkd, which berry does not depend on and which binds the keys that call
berryc.

 -- pkg.haus archive <archive@pkg.haus>
